# These files exist only for native iOS tooling (CocoaPods via `pod install`
# / EAS build) and aren't used by the web build at all. If Vercel's build
# container sees a Gemfile, it auto-runs `bundle install` before the actual
# build command, which fails here because the pinned Ruby version (see
# .ruby-version) isn't available on Vercel's build image. Excluding them
# from the upload keeps Vercel from ever detecting a Ruby project.
Gemfile
Gemfile.lock
.ruby-version
.bundle
